export_seq is a sequence number — it's just the order in which records were added to the database when they were exported.
Why is it leaking?
When data was exported, items that were returned might have been processed/flagged later
So returns are slightly clustered at certain export sequence numbers
This creates an artificial relationship between the sequence number and returns
In real production, you won't have this sequence number, or it will be meaningless
The model learns to use this "magic number" instead of real business features
Conclusion
This is a very simple example of a leakage problem, so we will remove export_seq from the model.